  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to the Green Climate Fund (GCF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The GCF was established under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change as the central mechanism for climate action. As the largest and highest profile climate fund, it is seen as a marker of international credibility on climate finance. As the world&#x2019;s largest climate fund, GCF accelerates transformative climate action in developing countries through a country-owned partnership approach and use of flexible financing solutions and climate investment expertise. By re-engaging we want to ensure climate finance works for those who are the most vulnerable to climate change, including for Pacific island countries.</narrative>
  </description>
